p Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Banned and Challenged Books, Censorship, General Interest, National Library Week ... Some students were restricted from exploring “the Great Perhaps.” John Green’s Looking for Alaska ranked No. 6 on the American Library Association’s Top Ten Challenged Books of 2016.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"039e7d98bd8b5064\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 13, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c03f6c366350e2d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c03f6c366350e2d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2aaaa4c9268c978\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBanned and challenged for profanity, drug use, and alcoholism, and because it was thought to promote anti-police views, contain divisive topics, and be “too much of a sensitive matter right now.” · Despite being taught in Somerset County Public School in Westover, MD, since 2016, All American Boys was challenged by a parent at a board meeting for its “foul and vulgar language” and “divisive topics.” The parent also challenged Ibram X.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2aaaa4c9268c978\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 5, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:oif.ala.org \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\" 2016", "provider": "brave", "count": 3, "tookMs": 810, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"34816d03457b9b8d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop Ten Challenged Books of 2016 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"34816d03457b