{"type": "message", "id": "0198b457", "parentId": "4c12e711", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:39:44.494Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_IItkiHtuJhfw19ZqoPsp5sXw", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:oif.ala.org \\\"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\\\" 2017 2018 2019\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 806,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5cd275faa9152e53\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Banned Book: Absolutely True Diary of a Part Time Indian - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5cd275faa9152e53\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/top-ten-banned-book-absolutely-true-diary-of-a-part-time-indian/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca40b760cbff9df9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian</strong> was the most-challenged book in the United States from 2010 to 2019 and was named one of the top ten most challenged books in 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2017, 2018, and 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca40b760cbff9df9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 29, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7b4430d039cbb41\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7b4430d039cbb41\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"293a0dfbb2c36593\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2020, more than 273 books were challenged or banned. Demands to remove books addressing racism and racial justice or those that shared the stories of Black, Indigenous, or people of color grew in number. At the same time, books addressing themes and issues of concern for LGBTQIA+ people continued to dominate the list.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"293a0dfbb2c36593\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 5, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cedc4965097956aa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2015 Top Ten Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cedc4965097956aa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=6397\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c628a13a38868d65\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom publishes the list of Top Ten Most Challenged Books. We collect information from two sources: newspapers and reports submitted by individuals. All challenges are compiled into a database. Reports of challenges culled from newspapers ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c628a13a38868d65\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2016\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28300cc3d12b4247\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTwelve Terrific Challenged LGBTQIAP+ Titles for Kids and Teens - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28300cc3d12b4247\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/twelve-terrific-challenged-lgbtqiap-titles-for-kids-and-teens/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a84658261a9addb8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile looking at the decade’s Top Ten Most Challenged Books and more expansive Frequently Challenged Books lists, the idea of creating a new list came to mind. In honor of Pride Month and ALA’s Rainbow Book Month, here is a list of Twelve Terrific Books that have ended up on these lists during the past decade. Haack, Daniel. Prince &amp; Knight, illustrated by Stevie Lewis, published by little bee books.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a84658261a9addb8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 29, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0c0a3c572f959ce8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Day in the Life of... ALA's Top 10 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0c0a3c572f959ce8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/a-day-in-the-life-of-alas-top-10-most-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15b500e6f0e4838f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom discusses the past year&#x27;s trends. Of the 566 books that were targeted in 2019, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15b500e6f0e4838f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 30, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2a2469246025f50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Challenged Books of 2016 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2a2469246025f50\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=9226\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4520338dc55ff68\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nApril 10, 2017April 20, 2017 Kristin Pekoll ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Banned and Challenged Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4520338dc55ff68\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 20, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc3a9cd72b4d5ace\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInterview with Jed Dearybury, LGBTQ+ Advocate - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc3a9cd72b4d5ace\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/interview-with-jed-dearybury-lgbtq-advocate/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb0ea0270b28c982\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOver half of the top 10 challenged books as reported by the ALA in 2018 included diverse content.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb0ea0270b28c982\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"May 25, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b22bb3a4ceb8aa2e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDefending Books in a Middle School: an Interview with Librarian Gina Schaarschmidt - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b22bb3a4ceb8aa2e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/q-facing-middle-school-book-challenge/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24643737cf4208df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn celebration of National Library Week and its theme “Libraries Lead,” the Intellectual Freedom Blog is highlighting the voices and experiences of fierce librarians who have defended the right to read in the past year. Learn more about the Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 and this year’s Banned Books Week theme “Banning Books Silences Stories; Speak Out!” at ala.org/bbooks/NLW-Top10.)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24643737cf4208df\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 8, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df6a7535a8f64612\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSpotlight on Censorship: 'Looking for Alaska' - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df6a7535a8f64612\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/spotlight-censorship-looking-alaska/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"30c8eb4269aa6cd9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe book was retained at Marion County High School, and many readers rejoiced. Looking for Alaska isn’t a stranger to ALA’s Top Ten list. The YA novel made the list in 2012, 2013 and 2015, with challenge reasonings listed as “offensive language,” “drugs/alcohol/smoking” and “unsuited to age group.”\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"30c8eb4269aa6cd9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 13, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c309b97dfcda6cab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDefining Diversity - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c309b97dfcda6cab\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/defining-diversity/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"67ad3facc20effa6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile “diversity” is seldom given as a reason for a challenge, it may in fact be an underlying and unspoken factor: the work is about people and issues others would prefer not to consider. Often, content addresses concerns of groups who have suffered historic and ongoing discrimination. For instance, a book that often recurs in previous years’ top ten challenges is Toni Morrison’s Beloved.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"67ad3facc20effa6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2016\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:oif.ala.org \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\" 2017 2018 2019", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 806, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT