{"type": "message", "id": "769cdf52", "parentId": "95247aa3", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:40:09.698Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_sQAFaNSYTlcEcMCf5KrISExC", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:oif.ala.org \\\"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\\\" 2018 April 2019\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 788,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1167e32c758c03b1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1167e32c758c03b1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f8366a87d41021a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nJoin us at Friday’s coffee chat with the authors of the #6 Most Challenged Book Something Happened in Our Town: A Child’s Story About Racial Injustice · Day-By-Day Guide to Celebrating National Library Week 2021 · Monday, April 5: State of America’s Libraries Report released, including Top Ten Frequently Challenged Books of 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f8366a87d41021a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 5, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1fc2cb0f9be83eb7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Banned Book: Absolutely True Diary of a Part Time Indian - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1fc2cb0f9be83eb7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/top-ten-banned-book-absolutely-true-diary-of-a-part-time-indian/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5fa7831a21330537\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian</strong> was the most-challenged book in the United States from 2010 to 2019 and was named one of the top ten most challenged books in 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2017, 2018, and 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5fa7831a21330537\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 29, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7a28de4cc405abf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTwelve Terrific Challenged LGBTQIAP+ Titles for Kids and Teens - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7a28de4cc405abf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/twelve-terrific-challenged-lgbtqiap-titles-for-kids-and-teens/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17056a2c861b423c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile looking at the decade’s Top Ten Most Challenged Books and more expansive Frequently Challenged Books lists, the idea of creating a new list came to mind. In honor of Pride Month and ALA’s Rainbow Book Month, here is a list of Twelve Terrific Books that have ended up on these lists during the past decade. Haack, Daniel. Prince &amp; Knight, illustrated by Stevie Lewis, published by little bee books.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17056a2c861b423c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 29, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"caea6adec775c248\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2015 Top Ten Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"caea6adec775c248\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=6397\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9904f7339003ea3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom publishes the list of Top Ten Most Challenged Books. We collect information from two sources: newspapers and reports submitted by individuals. All challenges are compiled into a database. Reports of challenges culled from newspapers ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9904f7339003ea3\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2016\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bc7319414c598b1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Day in the Life of... ALA's Top 10 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bc7319414c598b1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=20750\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"edd0602b6cceb1dd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe State of America’s Libraries report is an annual summary of library trends released during National Library Week that outlines statistics and issues affecting all types of libraries during the previous calendar year. This is when OIF releases the Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2019.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"edd0602b6cceb1dd\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 30, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:oif.ala.org \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\" 2018 April 2019", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 788, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1167e32c758c03b1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1167e32c758c03b1\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9f8366a87d41021a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nJoin