{"type": "message", "id": "586d4f8c", "parentId": "5870c65f", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:41:38.833Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_rkeyVMa01CfOPHMkKtc3Qm29", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:oif.ala.org \\\"challenged books of 2017\\\" \\\"Top Ten\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 757,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73c42b333c3949f7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Page 3 of 6 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73c42b333c3949f7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/category/ala-top-ten-most-frequently-challenged-books/page/3/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17b78c384f26a19e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA’s Office for Intellectual Freedom released its list of the Top 10 Most Challenged Books of 2016, and as usual, the majority of books are for children and teens. April 26, 2017April 24, 2017 Patricia Peters ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Banned and Challenged Books, Censorship, Library Bill of Rights, Minors\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17b78c384f26a19e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4e5d3b7c476755e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2017\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4e5d3b7c476755e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/ALAOIF_Field-Report-2017.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d9654d62e4171e7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nspot in the Top Ten Most Challenged Books list in · 2011 and 2009. Source: “Controversy over sexually explicit · book in Scottsdale school library,” Fox 10 · Phoenix, September 27, 2017. Olsson, Soren and Anders · Jacobsson · In Ned’s Head (2001) Challenged, after a fifth- grader checked out the ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d9654d62e4171e7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9e47a9071f8eaca\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Library Week Archives - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9e47a9071f8eaca\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/category/national-library-week/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57633d77fdacedf1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nApril 9, 2019April 11, 2019 Kristin Pekoll ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Authors, Banned and Challenged Books, Censorship, National Library Week · By: Robert Sarwark Trends Last week, the Top 10 Challenged Books of 2017 were announced by the Office for Intellectual Freedom.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57633d77fdacedf1\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da2b87773783a35e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBanned Books Week Coalition Declares that “Banning Books Silences Stories” - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da2b87773783a35e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/banned-books-week-coalition-declares-that-banning-books-silences-stories/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bc650f3c2df3270\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n“Tango has appeared on the ALA’s Most Challenged list for most of the dozen years since it was published,” says Parnell. “It’s a distinction we’re both proud of and wish didn’t exist. Thankfully, one powerful thing stands between our book and those who’ve tried to suppress it. It’s called the Constitution. Discretion is acceptable. Sensitivity is important. But censorship has no place in American public life.” · Drama has appeared in the Top 10 list three times now and is frequently challenged because it includes LGBTQ characters.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bc650f3c2df3270\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 12, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e02271385747b42c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDefending Books in a Middle School: an Interview with Librarian Gina Schaarschmidt - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e02271385747b42c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/q-facing-middle-school-book-challenge/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed2d4588bddf5a5c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn celebration of National Library Week and its theme “Libraries Lead,” the Intellectual Freedom Blog is highlighting the voices and experiences of fierce librarians who have defended the right to read in the past year. Learn more about the Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 and this year’s Banned Books Week theme “Banning Books Silences Stories; Speak Out!” at ala.org/bbooks/NLW-Top10.)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed2d4588bddf5a5c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 8, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:oif.ala.org \"challenged books of 2017\" \"Top Ten\"", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 757, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"73c42b333c3949f7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Page 3 of 6 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"73c42b333c3949f7\